# The Node floor is enforced here, not merely documented (#403).
#
# `package.json`'s `engines.node` is ADVISORY by default: npm prints a warning
# and installs anyway. So the floor this repo declares was not enforced anywhere
# a contributor would actually meet it — and the failure that produces is the
# one this codebase treats as worse than a crash. On Node 20, `jsdom`'s `undici`
# calls `webidl.util.markAsUncloneable`, which only exists on Node 22: every
# `web` test worker dies before running, and the suite prints green counts with
# a non-zero exit. Green counts over a run that checked nothing.
#
# `engine-strict` makes npm REFUSE to install instead, at the earliest possible
# moment, with the required range in the message. A wrong Node now degrades
# loudly, the way the collectors do.
#
# Verified rather than assumed, on 2026-08-16 (#403's own acceptance):
#
#   * a package declaring an unsatisfiable engine fails `npm install` with
#     `EBADENGINE` and prints both the required range and the version in use —
#     run against a scratch package, not reasoned from the docs;
#   * all 114 packages in this lockfile that declare `engines.node` are
#     satisfied by `22.22.2`, the exact version CI's min-node leg pins — scanned
#     with `semver.satisfies`, so this file cannot turn that leg red;
#   * `npm ci` completes with this file present.
engine-strict=true
